.TH CRS\-APP 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-app, crs\-provision\-desktop \- start DAQ applications with assigned
ports and generate their desktop icons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-app
.IR start | stop
.I app\-id
.br
.B crs\-app list
.br
.B crs\-provision\-desktop
.B \-\-session
.I NAME
.RB [ \-\-desktop\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B crs\-provision\-desktop \-\-all\-local
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crs\-app
runs on a DAQ host.
It reads
.BR ~/controlroom/etc/apps.yaml ,
exports
.BI CRS_PORT_ NAME
for every named port assigned to the application, then execs the
application's standardized
.BR start\- / stop\- script
(resolved in
.B ~/controlroom/bin
or the app's
.IR install_path ).
.B DISPLAY
is inherited, so icons inside a VNC desktop launch apps onto that
session's display.
.PP
.B crs\-provision\-desktop
writes
.IB app \-start.desktop
/
.IB app \-stop.desktop
launchers (calling crs\-app) into
.B ~/Desktop
for every application that apps.yaml assigns to the given session.
With
.B \-\-all\-local
it derives the session list from controlroom.yaml entries matching this
host and
.BR $USER .
.PP
Both tools are stdlib-only and fall back to a restricted built-in YAML
parser when PyYAML is not installed on the host.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
    crs\-app list
    crs\-app start dashboard
    crs\-provision\-desktop \-\-all\-local
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR install\-controlroom (1)
